{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_positivity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_positivity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_binet","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L98-L103","doc":"Restatement of the exclusion in the form the probe asserts: a positive\nreadout is nonzero, so every two-step ratio `φ(n+2)/φ(n)` is finite and\ngoverned by `linFunctionalK_two_step`.  No division by a near-node. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovReadout_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovReadout_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L87-L96","doc":"**The canonical Markov-trace readout has no node.**\n\n`tr_M(1) = 1` and `tr_M(σ₀) = z > 0`, so the readout the framework\nactually derives is positive at every winding.  Combined with\n`linFunctionalK_two_step`, its generation tower is log-linear up to the\n`O(q⁻²ⁿ)` remainder — it cannot be bent to the observed log-concave\nlepton tower, and the node escape is not available to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L74-L85","doc":"**Every positive readout is strictly positive — it has no node.**\n\n`φ(1) ≥ 0` and `φ(σ₀) > 0` suffice.  This is the invariant that\nforecloses the node escape described above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L70-L72","doc":"**The continuant never vanishes on the physical range.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_nonneg_and_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_nonneg_and_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L54-L68","doc":"The continuant is non-negative, and strictly positive from index `1`.\n\nBoth halves are needed simultaneously: the recurrence\n`b_{n+2} = h b_{n+1} + b_n` derives positivity of `b_{n+2}` from strict\npositivity of `b_{n+1}` together with non-negativity of `b_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hecke_h_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hecke_h_pos","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_positivity.lean#L47-L52","doc":"For `q > 1` the Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹` is positive. ","signatureChunk":0}]}